Pi_Swift text-chat development dependency
----------------------------------------

MemoshiCore's MemoshiRuntime consumes Pi_Swift unmodified, at the annotated tag
slice-2, from a clean checkout of that commit, not from any working directory:

  https://github.com/mehmetcanbudak/Pi_Swift
  tag slice-2, revision ce1728ef8236d95a8b94b50a856670c48ad85365
  upstream Pi revision 22dc6c26f3c530e11b8cc40443ecdce2b3c84116

scripts/check-prerequisites.sh creates that checkout (../Pi_Swift-slice-2) from the
sibling Pi_Swift Git repository and refuses it unless it is exactly that commit
with no change. SwiftPM uses it by path: slice-2's manifest has a local package
dependency, which SwiftPM does not allow under a revision pin. Memoshi's adapter
is original source; Pi modules remain external dependencies. SubscriptionLogins
is not enabled. No Pi terminal/CLI product is linked.

MemoshiRuntime links PiCodeMode and PiMCP, both part of the same Pi_Swift
revision, for an explicit development/qualification composition only; the
normal app and daemon composition installs no Code Mode, MCP or other tools.
PiCodeMode carries the pinned QuickJS guest both as WebAssembly (run by WasmKit)
and translated to C by WABT 1.0.42 wasm2c with WABT's runtime; PiAI carries a
pinned Zstandard codec. Pi_Swift's own third-party notices, including these, ship
unmodified in PiCore's resource bundle (ThirdPartyNotices.txt). The guest's
upstream licence resources remain unmodified.

Resolved additional dependencies:
  WasmKit 0.4.2, revision a7455cb8474b96b2c58f0adc1f70d0270b8010bf, MIT.
  Swift Syntax 604.0.0, revision 050f1a346fbbac0ca2cfb15a95274f7bd1cf0ccf,
    https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-syntax
  Swift Argument Parser 1.8.2, revision 6a52f3251125d74daf04fcbd5e6f08a75d074382,
    https://github.com/apple/swift-argument-parser
The latter two retain Apache 2.0 WITH the Runtime Library Exception, not plain
